### Market Oracle API Tests
### 
### NOTE: API keys must be configured in .env file (never in request body for security)
### All configuration fields in requests are optional - API keys come from .env
###
### WORKFLOW (3 Steps):
### 1. Call /validate endpoint with YouTube URLs (returns analysis_id and validation results)
### 2. Call /analyze endpoint with analysis_id and optional economic calendar config
### 3. Call /process endpoint with analysis_id to get CSV data and full analysis

### Variables
@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000
@analysisId = 20251220_212438
### ^ Update this variable with the analysis_id from /validate response

### ============================================================================
### GET STATUS
### ============================================================================

GET {{baseUrl}}/
Content-Type: application/json

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 1: VALIDATE YOUTUBE TRANSCRIPTS (Returns analysis_id)
### ============================================================================

### Validate YouTube URLs - Multiple URLs
### This is the FIRST endpoint to call. It validates YouTube URLs, extracts transcripts,
### creates an analysis directory, and returns validation results with analysis_id.
### 
### IMPORTANT: Copy the "analysis_id" value and use it in the /analyze endpoint!
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jNQXAC9IVRw",
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9bZkp7q19f0"
  ]
}

###

### Validate YouTube URLs - Single URL (for testing)
POST {{baseUrl}}/validate
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "youtube_urls": [
    "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dQw4w9WgXcQ"
  ]
}

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 2: RUN ANALYSIS (Requires analysis_id from /validate)
### ============================================================================

### Run Analysis - Minimal (Only analysis_id, uses defaults from .env)
### NOTE: This endpoint requires analysis_id from /validate endpoint.
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}"
}

###

### Run Analysis - With Full Configuration
POST {{baseUrl}}/analyze
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "forexfactory_start_date": "2025-12-14",
  "forexfactory_use_week": true,
  "tradingeconomics_start_date": "2025-12-15",
  "tradingeconomics_end_date": "2025-12-21"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### STEP 3: PROCESS ANALYSIS (Generate CSV from analysis_id)
### ============================================================================

### Process Analysis - Generate CSV
### IMPORTANT: Update @analysisId variable at the top of this file with the analysis_id from /validate response
### This endpoint will:
### - Read comprehensive_analysis.txt from the analysis directory
### - Generate CSV data from the analysis
### - Return both CSV data and full comprehensive analysis
POST {{baseUrl}}/process
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}"
}

###

### ============================================================================
### ADDITIONAL ENDPOINTS
### ============================================================================

### Ask AI about a specific event
### Uses web search to provide current information about an event
POST {{baseUrl}}/ask-ai
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "question": "What is the current status of this event?",
  "event": {
    "Token": "Bitcoin",
    "Date": "2025-12-25",
    "Event_Type": "Listed",
    "Title": "Fed Interest Rate Decision",
    "Event_Description": "Federal Reserve interest rate decision"
  },
  "analysis_id": "{{analysisId}}",
  "max_searches": 5,
  "max_tokens": 4000
}

###

### Web Search - Basic Example
### Performs a web search using the AI API (Anthropic or OpenRouter)
POST {{baseUrl}}/websearch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "What are the latest Bitcoin price predictions for 2025?",
  "max_searches": 5,
  "max_tokens": 4000
}

###

### Web Search - With Domain Filtering (Anthropic Only)
### Restricts search to trusted financial news sources
### Note: Domain filtering only works with Anthropic API, not OpenRouter
POST {{baseUrl}}/websearch
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "prompt": "What are the latest Bitcoin and XRP price predictions and market analysis?",
  "allowed_domains": [
    "coindesk.com",
    "cointelegraph.com",
    "bloomberg.com",
    "reuters.com",
    "cnbc.com",
    "forbes.com"
  ],
  "max_searches": 5,
  "max_tokens": 4000
}

###
